  "title": "Murasaki Shikibu, author of The Tale of Genji",
  "summary": "Murasaki Shikibu, a noblewoman of Japan's Heian period whose real name is unknown, wrote The Tale of Genji, widely considered one of the world's first novels. Around 1005 Fujiwara no Michinaga brought her to court to serve his daughter, Empress Shoshi. She also left a diary. Her birth is placed around 973 or 978, and her death between 1013 and about 1030.",
